Error [E0105]: method `encode` is defined twice on `Bad`
  --> tests/ui/serde_generated_cascade_keeps_user_impl_error.jet:3:5
    |
  3 | #[Encode]
    |     ^^^^^
 Why: each method name may appear only once on a type
 Fix: rename or remove one of the definitions

Error [E0908]: `Bad` already implements `Encode`
  --> tests/ui/serde_generated_cascade_keeps_user_impl_error.jet:1:6
    |
  1 | struct Plain {}
    |      ^^^
 Why: each type may implement a trait only once
 Fix: remove the duplicate `impl` block

Error [E2411]: `Plain` can't be serialized
  --> tests/ui/serde_generated_cascade_keeps_user_impl_error.jet:5:5
    |
  5 |     inner: Plain
    |     ^^^^^
 Why: only types that opt in (and their fields) have a wire form; `Plain` does not
 Fix: add `#[Codable]` or `#[Encode]` to `Plain`, or remove it from the encoded value

Error [E0113]: `encode` promises to return `DataTree`, but this returns Int (a whole number)
  --> tests/ui/serde_generated_cascade_keeps_user_impl_error.jet:10:16
    |
 10 |         return 1
    |                ^
 Why: the value handed back must match the type after `->`
 Fix: use `DataTree` here
